{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990596-mages-becoming-other-supernatural-beings","id":990596,"title":"Mages becoming other supernatural beings","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-20T13:36:55-07:00","id":990596,"title":"Mages becoming other supernatural beings","content":"So, we have legacies that are focused around ultimately allowing the Mage to become another sort of being, for immortality, power, etc. I believe the main examples are the legacy that turns its practicioners into spirits, and the mages from Astral Realms who turn into astral entities. And we've had some mages turning into ghosts/undead entities. What are some other possibilities for this? Could an Acanthus legacy eventually turn its members into True Fae? Maybe a Moros legacy with the end goal of turning mages into Kerberos-like beings or deathlords? An Obrimos legacy that aims to turn Mages into some type of angelic being? I could see a Mastigos legacy ending with the Mage becoming something quite like a Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T13:52:32-07:00","id":990611,"title":"","content":"I think there is a legacy about turning into angels, but I forget their name. Scions of God?<br /> <br /> Also there is the idea of Ascension, where one turns into a supernal symbol.<br /> <br /> I suppose a Fang of Mara could be considered closer to a Beast than a standard mage. There's a neat Scelestus Legacy that starts replacing their body parts and organs with Abyssal entities. With the new Legacy system you could take that further.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T14:35:49-07:00","id":990636,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the scions are the spirit ones. I reread them, and they see their transformation into spirits as becoming &quot;angelic&quot;. Plenty of room for other legacies that focus on other types of angelic beings, or spirit transformation from another perspective.<br /> <br /> Oh, here's one- a Thyrsus legacy that binds an animal (or other) spirit to their soul, making them sort of a pseudo-werewolf/pseudo-claimed. Gameplaywise, this means they get a set of transformations they can use as an Attainment. If it seems unbalanced, remember that Life lets a Mage turn into a regenerating monster anyway- making it an attainment just makes that specific application easier to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T15:39:32-07:00","id":990665,"title":"","content":"Well, there's a Thyrsus Legacy from Summoners that sort of does that, gaining spirit powers like Influences and so on. And there's the Daksha that turn into three-eyed hermaphrodites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T17:12:02-07:00","id":990694,"title":"","content":"If the point is the possibility, not necessarily what we already know, so that depends on what you call one of those beings. A Legacy can give the Mage some characteristics of those creatures, whyle the Mage can use her own magic to achieve similar status. But hardly a Legacy can do the work of turning into some creatures by itself. And certainly not gaining the same mechanics, they would still work mostly as Mages.<br /> <br /> So, what is a True Fae for you? Or a Kerberos? Or any particular splat?<br /> <br /> Declare how much characteristics of those beings you would want to classify the character as such, and we can work it around. But simply add the &quot;template&quot; by meas of a Legacy will hardly be possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T10:06:14-07:00","id":991425,"title":"","content":"I think there are limits to what you can become. No True Fae, because no Mage has the power to summon, create, and control True Fae.<br /> <br /> No Changeling, again because they can't create, summon, or control Changelings like they can Ghosts, Goetics, and Spirits.<br /> <br /> No Werewolves <br /> <br /> No Vampires, trying is how the Treme happened.<br /> <br /> Claimed, yes.<br /> <br /> Sin Eaters, no for the same reason.<br /> <br /> Supernal Beings I'd say and in fact of the Lich legacies I could see ones that transform you into a Supernal Being as the most common and closest to being respectible.<br /> <br /> Godmachine Angel, maybe, use your soul and body as parts to build a new Angel, but the Legacy would need access to infastructure.<br /> <br /> Strix no.<br /> <br /> Hobgoblins yes, even though they don't command, summon, or create Hobgoblins, being trapped in the Hedge can eventually do that by its self, so its just about shaping your soul so that you retain memories and arcana during the process.<br /> <br /> Deviant no, because once your soul is cracked I don't think it'd be good for Supernal Magic any more.<br /> <br /> Pangaean, with great difficulty, yes, but only if you gain access to the heart of an Ancient Pangaean to create the Legacy.<br /> <br /> Cthothian yes, simular to ghosts.<br /> <br /> Prommies, maybe.<br /> <br /> Pandorans, why would you want to?<br /> <br /> Abssyal being yes.<br /> <br /> Mummy no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T10:32:24-07:00","id":991435,"title":"","content":"I mean, for me, &quot;would this be a fun story&quot; always takes precedence over any Watsonian concerns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T10:35:37-07:00","id":991436,"title":"","content":"EDIT: Wrong thread, d'oh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-22-2016, 04:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T13:39:48-07:00","id":991508,"title":"","content":"Who did that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T13:46:21-07:00","id":991515,"title":"","content":"Damn it, wrong thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T12:45:04-07:00","id":991958,"title":"","content":"For immortality, what about becoming a ghoul? A little Mind could easily counteract any addiction or Vinculum gained along the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T13:02:17-07:00","id":991971,"title":"","content":"As far as I remember, in CoD it isn't possible for a Major Template to take on <u>any</u> other Template, so it isn't possible to ghouling a Mage.<br /> <br /> That said, vampiric blood could be a thing for a spell or Legacy to use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}